Medium grain rice seeds are defined as certified planting material that yields grains shorter than the long grain category yet longer than short grain varieties, such as the globally recognized Calrose, Koshihikari, and Momi Rosa strains. These seeds are prized for their balanced aroma, texture, and high yield potential, and they are increasingly adopted by commercial farms to meet evolving consumer preferences for sticky and aromatic rice dishes.
